<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-20994] osd-ldiskfs: end bios on RAID row boundaries</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20994</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;osd_do_bio() fills each bio until the disk blocks stop being contiguous or bio_add_folio() refuses the next page. Where a full bio ends then depends on how many of the I/O buffer pages merge into multi-page bvecs, not on the RAID geometry, so on RAID OSTs it usually ends in the middle of a row (full stripe). The RAID layer receives that row in two bios and has to take its partial-stripe path for it: read-modify-write, or a slower stripe-cache path instead of a full-row write.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Seen on md RAID6 8+2 OSTs with a 128 KiB chunk (1 MiB rows) under 4 MiB O_DIRECT writes: about half of the requests reached md as 2-4 bios cut mid-row, and 23% of rows were written as partial stripes. Tracing block_bio_queue on the md device shows bios ending at arbitrary offsets within a row.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The ldiskfs stripe (mount -o stripe=, or the superblock stripe width/stride set by mkfs -E stride=,stripe_width=) already gives the row size. Proposal: for writes, at each row boundary end the bio when the next row (or the rest of the I/O) will not fit in the bvecs left in it, counting the bvecs from the row's pages so bios still span several rows when pages merge. Reads and OSTs without a stripe are unchanged.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;With the patch on the site above, 100% of rows were written as full stripes, and client writes improved by 26% (2 OSTs on one server) and 7% (4 OSTs on two servers).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Related:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20564" title="Probe md RAID geometry so OST ldiskfs allocations align to full stripes" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20564"&gt;LU-20564&lt;/a&gt; (mkfs.lustre probes md geometry): sets the stripe width this change relies on, for OSTs where mke2fs cannot derive it. That aligns block allocation to rows; this change aligns the bios that write them.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20199" title="A large RPC is queued as numerous bios" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20199"&gt;LU-20199&lt;/a&gt; (higher-order I/O buffers): reduces bio fragmentation from the bvec limit. Independent of this change, which keeps bios row-aligned at any bio size.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</description>
